  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan treats the Refinement Path Convention as a grand event that concerns the Infallible inheritance and begins collecting Gu refinement materials so he can compete for its rewards.",
      "chapters": [
        734
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_refinement_path_convention"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During the convention he knows the inheritance has hidden requirements: the more Gu Masters that participate, the better.",
      "chapters": [
        831
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A good final ranking qualifies a participant for the inheritance’s reward.",
      "chapters": [
        836
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Infallible inheritance is a refinement path inheritance. Central Continent’s Refinement Path Convention began as a way for the ten great ancient sects to fight over it and split its benefits by refinement competition; because its benefits were too great and could even help recover fate Gu, Heavenly Court took it over. Fang Yuan judges that he needs at least top six to benefit.",
      "chapters": [
        838
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "convention-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent",
        "fac_ten_great_sects",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "fac_heavenly_court"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Being named infallible means no failure in Gu refinement. Fang Yuan’s target for that assured-success chance is refining change form Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        843
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "name-meaning",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_change_form_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Heavenly Court rank eights open Infallible blessed land over Hairy Foot Mountain, Lian Jiu Sheng names it as the land that holds the Infallible inheritance. Heaven Overseeing Tower Lord reports that Heavenly Court has pressed the land for thousands of years and can take only thirty success dao marks when the inheritance accumulates to a thirty-six mark limit, leaving six for Refinement Path Convention participants that Heavenly Court cannot seize. Heavenly Court research ties the land to the hairy man leader: the inheritance gathers other people’s failures into mortal failure Gu, then condenses them into success dao marks; Heavenly Court used the land and the convention to accumulate those marks toward restoring fate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        845
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "land-and-dao-marks",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_infallible_blessed_land",
        "loc_hairy_foot_mountain",
        "char_lian_jiu_sheng",
        "char_heaven_overseeing_tower_lord",
        "race_hairy_men",
        "gu_failure_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "One success dao mark can at most remove failure probability for rank six Immortal Gu refinement; rank seven and rank eight need more than one. Major technique errors can still fail the refinement, and uniqueness of Immortal Gu can still block success if the target already exists.",
      "chapters": [
        847
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "success-mark-limits",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan uses up the success dao mark from the Infallible inheritance while refining change form Immortal Gu, along with almost all of his immortal materials and immortal essence stones. Separately, Yu Mu Chun also uses a success dao mark from the inheritance and notes that these marks are closely related to refinement path, unlike ordinary success dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        862
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "success-mark-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yu_mu_chun"
      ]
    }
  ],
